-- title:
--   Transported ℓ-level agrees under an e_γ-translate of a rigidification
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), and $N$ is a nonzero squarefree integer (`hN`) divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`).
--
--   **Base rings (`hdvr`–`hvdet`).** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), with that ideal maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it (`hFr`). Finally $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism characterised by $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli (`hB`–`harbar`).** $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for each finite place $v$ the completion is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or $\bar r$), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal order (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ together with a point map `pt` on fake elliptic curves (relative abelian surfaces with commutative group law, $\Lambda$-action subject to the trace condition, and level-$N$ data) is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ is prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), and $M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` is a fine moduli space for full level $n$ (`hM`), carrying an action $\rho$ of a group $G$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ realising level twists (`hρ`). The forgetful map $p : M \to \mathcal X$ lies over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and matches the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptT` is a coarse moduli space for curves with an extra level subgroup of order $\ell^{2}$ (`h𝒴`), and $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ are the two degeneracy maps over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), $d_0$ forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ recording the $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). Maps $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over $f$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side (`hdef`–`hwbar`).** $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); $n_1$ is an adelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) with $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and $v$ is the place of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ consists of the units which are local units of $R_1$ at every place other than $v$ (`hΓt`). Elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $s_{f,\ell}$ satisfy (`hs`, four clauses): $s_{f,\ell}$ equals $s_\ell$ at all places not above $r$, equals $1$ at the places above $r$, the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1, R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; the groups $\tilde\Gamma_\ell = \tilde\Gamma \cap s_\ell \tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$ are fixed by `hΓtℓ`. The unit $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Coordinates on $\Lambda$.** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ (values in $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$) is an order coordinate system (`hcoord`): additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule, injective, with dense image, and compatible with traces.
--
--   **Special fibre (`hX₀`–`hE5e`).** $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of dimension $2$ over that ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of formal coordinates for $A_0$, and `hA₀` says the formal group of $A_0$ is $X_0$ with $\Lambda$ acting through $\mathrm{coord}$. Maps $e, e' : \tilde\Gamma \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ lie over the base (`he`) and, with degrees $\deg$, satisfy: each pair $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ data (`hE1`); multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e_\gamma$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$ (`hE1mul`); scalars $\gamma$ give scalar $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE1sc`) and conversely (`hE1'`); for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ (`hE2`); the action of $\tilde\Gamma$ on a full level-$n$ structure is by $\Lambda$-labels, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$ (`hE3`); and every $r$-power self-isogeny of a geometric fibre of $A_0$ preserving the level comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE4`). An order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r^{c}R_1 \subseteq R_2$ for suitable exponents (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) acts by $\hat e$ over the base (`hê`), additively, $\Lambda$-equivariantly and level-preservingly (`hE5a`), unitally and multiplicatively with integers acting by $\Lambda$-multiplication (`hE5b1`–`hE5b3`), with $\hat e_{\bar x}\hat e_x = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$ (`hE5c`), compatibly with $e$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE5d`), and jointly with $e$ realised on formal coordinates by a single conjugating matrix (`hE5e`).
--
--   **Formal moduli package and uniformisation (`hΦ`–`hPiexD`).** $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$, special relative to $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); $MD$ is a moduli package satisfying the Zariski sheaf axiom (`hMD`); $\eta$ assigns $MD$-points to rigidified formal modules, and `hη` (three clauses) says that on admissible objects $\eta$ identifies points exactly with isomorphism classes, is natural in the base ring, and is surjective after passing to a Zariski cover. $E_0$ is an injective ring map from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is squeezed between $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ and $r^{-m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ for some $m$ (`hE₀`). On Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, $e_D$ is a map from the $G$-points of $MD$ to the product of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}, -)$ with the Deligne datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$; it is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), has first component the structural leg (`hfstD`), converts the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action on Deligne data (`hGLD`), converts $\pi$-translations into Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`). A ring map $\kappa : O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ is compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny $\Phi \to \kappa_*X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on $A_0$ consist of $A_{0,w}$ with $a_w, a_w'$ an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`) and $b_w, b_w'$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` realises, for a single conjugating matrix, the $e_\gamma$ as in `hE2` together with $a_w \!\gg\! b_w$ corresponding to $\iota_0(\bar w)$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$ (`hΞleg`–`hC3`).** $\Xi$ sends a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, relative to $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, to a $G$-point of $MD$; over connected $B$ its leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ (`hΞleg`); it is natural under pullback of rigidifications (`hΞnat`); it is unchanged under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the auxiliary data up to powers of $r$ (`hΞiso`); and over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent it is computed by $\eta$ from a rigidified formal module transported from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with twist exponent $j \leq 1$, admissible after the Frobenius twist by $-j$ (`hΞdef`). With $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ fixed: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds, up to a power of $r$, to the action of $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $MD$-points (`heqΓ`), and the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds likewise to $g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`). The clauses `hK1`–`hK4` say that, for the leg $\psi$ twisted by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)$ and the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action, every Deligne datum point is realised by some pair (curve, rigidification) (`hK1`), any two such realisations are isomorphic with matching rigidifications up to powers of $r$ (`hK2`), realisations are stable under base change (`hK3`), and they lift along surjections with kernel of square zero, without changing which Deligne data they match (`hK4`). The normalised transport of $P_0$ to a full level-$n$ structure along a rigidification exists (`hC0e`) and is unique on underlying points (`hC0u`). The map $\Theta_f$ carries $(\psi, P, g)$ to nilpotent points of $M$, naturally (`hnat`) and $G$-equivariantly (`hG`), and matches the fine moduli point of the realised curve with its transported level structure (`hC2`) and, after composing with $p$, the coarse moduli point of the curve (`hC2c`). Finally $\theta_t : \tilde\Gamma \to G$ is a homomorphism, and `hC3` describes the effect of the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action: a new rigidification with the right leg and evaluation exists, its transported level-$n$ structure is the $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$-twist of the old one, and at primes $\ell \neq r$ invertible in the base the extra levels transported from an $e_\gamma$-stable extra level of $A_0$ agree.
--
--   **The geometric-point situation.** $k$ is an algebraically closed field and $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hk`), $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and $P, P'$ are Deligne data over $k$. Write $\psi^{\dagger}$ for the Frobenius twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$-precomposition of $\psi$. There are fake elliptic curves $E, E'$ over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho$ of $E$ and $\varrho'$ of $E'$ relative to $\psi^{\dagger}$ such that the legs of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ and $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ are $\psi^{\dagger}$ (`hΞψ`, `hΞψ'`) and their images under $e_D$ are related to $(\psi,P)$, respectively $(\psi,P')$, by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action (`hev`, `hev'`); there is an isomorphism $i : E \cong E'$ over $k$ (`hi`) compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-action and the level-$N$ data (`hvia`). Moreover $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ (`hγ`), and $\varrho''$ is a further rigidification of $E$ relative to $\psi^{\dagger}$ whose $\Xi$-leg is $\psi^{\dagger}$ and whose $e_D$-image matches $(\psi,P')$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action (`hev''`), the pairs $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ being related by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ (`htw`). Finally $\varrho''$ is the $e_\gamma$-translate of $\varrho$ (`htr`: there is a comparison of the two rigidifications together with a lift $e_{\gamma b}$ of $e_\gamma$ making the two $r$-power isogenies agree after multiplication by powers of $r$), and $\varrho''$ corresponds to $\varrho'$ along $i$ (`hcorr`: there are $i_b$ on the reductions with $i_b \!\gg\! \varrho'.g_b = \varrho''.g_b \!\gg\! i$ and $i_b$ over the base, a pullback comparison $u_A$ of the $A_0$-legs with $u_A \!\gg\! \varrho''.g_A = \varrho'.g_A$, and exponents $i_1, j_1$ with $i_b \!\gg\! \varrho'.\varphi \!\gg\! u_A \!\gg\! [r^{i_1}] = \varrho''.\varphi \!\gg\! [r^{j_1}]$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \neq r$ whose image in $k$ is a unit, and every extra level $\mathcal K$ of $A_0$ at $\ell$ (a finite flat $\Lambda$-stable subgroup scheme of rank $\ell^{2}$, disjoint from the level-$N$ subscheme; written `K₀` in the conclusion) which is stable under $e_\gamma$, in the sense that for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$ factoring through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$, the point $R \!\gg\! e_{\langle\gamma,h\gamma\rangle}$ again factors through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$: for all extra levels $C$ and $C'$ of $E$ at $\ell$ such that
--
--   (i) for every scheme $T$, every $t' : T \to \operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$, the existence of $R_0 : T \to C.K$ with $R_0$ followed by $C.\mathrm{levK}$ equal to $R$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$ implies the existence of $Q_0 : T \to \mathcal K.K$ with $Q_0$ followed by $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$ equal to $R$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ and then $\varrho.g_A$; and
--
--   (ii) the same condition for $C'$ with $\varrho$ replaced throughout by $\varrho''$,
--
--   it follows that for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, the point $R$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$ if and only if it factors through $C'.\mathrm{levK}$.
--
--   This is the agreement half of the extra-level transport statement in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: at a geometric point of the formal fibre it asserts that the extra level at a prime $\ell \neq r$ pulled back from an $e_\gamma$-stable extra level of the special fibre $A_0$ does not depend on whether the rigidification is replaced by its $e_\gamma$-translate. It is used by the combined statement which adds the stability clause, and thereby in the verification that the uniformisation respects the Hecke correspondences away from $r$ and $\bar r$. The proof cites the three facts about extra levels: their pullback along a pullback of fake elliptic curves, their unique transport along an $r$-power isogeny at a prime $\ell \neq r$ invertible in the base, and the étale description of points of an extra level when $\ell$ is invertible.
